    "FAIL": "At least one fully validated supported finding contains a nonempty availableInventoryItemId in the matched collected assessment.",
    "PASS": "One complete, source-bound, timestamped assessment matches the exact VM and has no nonempty available fix references; unknown fields/severities and incomplete inventory cannot produce this verdict.",
    "UNKNOWN": "Missing/denied/partial/malformed/future reports or contexts, unproved project numeric aliases, unsafe or ambiguous subject joins, unsupported severity/model, missing fix item shape or source authority.",
    "empty_report_boundary": "No reports or an empty object cannot pass. A complete generated report with name/updateTime, subject authority and empty vulnerabilities list can describe assessed zero findings; it is not an absence-of-report pass.",
    "omission_boundary": "The source producer maps an omitted availableInventoryItemId to a present key with None using dict.get; None/empty string mean no available fix reference in this native projection. Malformed non-string non-null references and missing normalized keys are UNKNOWN.",
    "timestamp_boundary": "Compare RFC3339 assessment updateTime <= native report collected_at <= snapshot created_at at nanosecond precision. No age threshold, freshness verdict or wall-clock decision is introduced.",
    "projection_limit": "The existing producer strips CVE/details, first-observation time and full package metadata. Counts are returned finding rows and fix references, not distinct CVEs, package ages or installation dates.",
    "no_normative_policy_input": true,
    "no_os_inventory_package_join": true
  },
